{[show NS]

[showcards W:D3] South is to play 3NT. West leads the \D3.

Make a Plan, then choose dummy's card to this trick. [choose-card DA]



[showcards E:DT S:D2] East plays the \D10 and you the \D2.

Winners:   \S = 1    \H = 5  \D = 1    \C = 1 Total = 8

You need just one more winner. Since West probably has 4 \Ds you will not be able to establish a trick in that suit, so your only hope is the \SQ. You win the first \D so they don't get a chance to switch to \Cs, a suit you are worse off in. Then take your 5 \H tricks, ending in dummy.

Click NEXT. [NEXT]

[PLAY W:D3,E:DT,S:D2,N:HA,E:H3,S:H6,W:H2,N:HK,E:H5,S:HT,W:H8,N:HQ,E:H7,S:S7,W:H9,N:HJ,E:C5,S:C4,W:C7,N:H4,E:CT,S:C3,W:C9]



You can't put it off any longer. Which card do you lead from dummy? [choose-card any:S9,S8,S6]

[showcards E:S2]

East plays low. Which card do you play? [choose-card SQ]

[showcards W:S3]

A small \S from dummy, putting the \SQ on. If it wins you will make your contract, if it loses you won't.

Click NEXT to find out which. [NEXT]

[show NESW]

[clear-commentary]

East held the \SK so you were lucky this time.

But remember, finesses only work half the time. The other half they lose.}
