[Student "S"]
{[show NS]

[showcards W:HQ N:H2 E:H3] South is to play 3NT. West leads the \HQ, dummy plays the \H2 and East the \H3.

Make a Plan, then play a card from your hand. [choose-card any:HK,HA]



Winners:   \S = 0    \H = 2  \D = 2    \C = 4 Total = 8

Needing one more winner you should see right away that it cannot come from \Hs, \Ds, or \Cs. That means you must hope that East has the \SA. Win the first \H, then play your 4 \C winners ending in dummy.

Click NEXT. [NEXT]

[PLAY W:HQ,N:H2,E:H3,S:CA,W:C3,N:C2,E:C4,S:CQ,W:C6,N:C5,E:C9,S:C8,W:CT,N:CJ,E:D2,N:CK,E:H5,S:C7,W:D4]



The moment of truth. Which card do you lead from dummy? [choose-card any:S6,S5,S3]

[showcards E:S4]

East plays low. Which card do you play? [choose-card SK]

[showcards W:SA]

A small \S from dummy, and the \SK when East plays low.

Unfortunately West takes your \SK with the \SA. He then plays another \H and you at least make 8 tricks but have no hope for a ninth one so you go down 1.

Click NEXT to see the bad news. [NEXT]

[show NESW]

[clear-commentary]

You probably thought since these Deals were all about finesses that they would work all of the time.

Welcome to the real world.}
[Play "W"]
