{[show NS]

[showcards W:SK N:S2 E:S5] South is to play 4\H. West leads the \SK, dummy plays the \S2 and East the \S5.

Make a Plan, then play a card from your hand. [choose-card SA]



Losers:   \S = 2    \H = 1  \D = 0    \C = 1 Total = 4

West found the best opening lead for his side, exposing your \S losers before you could establish the \C suit for a discard. If you start to pull trumps right away the defense will grab the \HA, then take their two \S tricks and you will still have the \CA that you cannot avoid.

Other than the \DA the only useful card in dummy is the \DQ so you must try to make a winner out of that for a  discard. [PLAY W:SK,N:S2,E:S5]

You won the \SA. Which card do you lead now? [choose-card D8]

[showcards W:D5]

West plays low. Which card do you play from dummy? [choose-card DQ]

[showcards E:D2]

Win the \SA, lead your singleton \D and finesse the \DQ. Your luck has returned, the \DQ wins. [NEXT]

[PLAY W:D5,E:D2] [showcards N:DA E:D3]

Dummy leads the \DA and East follows. Which card do you discard? [choose-card any:S7,S4]

[showcards W:D6]

You discard one of your \S losers on the \DA.

Click NEXT. [NEXT]

[PLAY N:DA,E:D3,W:D6]



At this point you have not lost any tricks, and you can see that you have only 3 losers remaining in your hand. So you start pulling trumps and establishing the \Cs.

Clickfor the complete deal. [NEXT]

[RESET]

[show NESW]

[clear-commentary]

If the \D finesse had lost you would have gone down 2 instead of just one.

The risk was worthwhile though since it gave you your only chance of making the contract.}
[Play "W"]
