{[show NS]

South is to play 4\S. West leads the \H5. The defense wins 3 \H tricks, then switches to a \D.

Make a Plan, then click NEXT. [NEXT]

[PLAY W:H5,N:H6,E:HQ,S:H2,E:HA,S:H4,W:H8,N:H9,E:H3,S:H7,W:HK,N:HT,W:D4,N:D5,E:D2,S:DK]



Losers:   \S = ?    \H = 3  \D = 0    \C = 0 Total = 3 ?

You have already lost the 3 \H tricks so you must pick up the trump suit without loss. Which card do you lead? [choose-card any:S6,S5,S3]

[showcards W:S2]

West plays low. Which card do you play from dummy? [choose-card SJ]

[showcards E:S8]

The odds aren't in your favor, but you have no choice but to play West for the doubleton King.



So: a small \S from your hand, putting on the \SJ when West plays low. When this holds the trick plunk down the \SA and hope.

Clickfor the complete Deal to see if the \SK dropped or not. [NEXT]

[RESET]

[show NESW]

[clear-commentary]

This position is one that is misplayed very often.

Look what would have occurred if you had started with the \SQ. West would have covered with the \SK (if he had it) and you would have lost a trick to the \ST later. 

The only hope is to try to drop the \SK without wasting an extra honor.}
[Play "W"]
