{[show NS]

[showcards W:HQ N:H5 E:H2] South is to play 6\S after North's Stayman bid. West leads the \HQ, dummy plays the \H5 and East the \H2.

Make a Plan, then play a card from your hand. [choose-card HA]



Losers:   \S = 0    \H = 1  \D = 0    \C = 1 Total = 2

This looks like a very simple plan. Since the hands have mirrored distribution there will be no discards anywhere. That means the \CK <b>MUST</b> be in West's hand or you will go down. But is that all there is to it?

[PLAY W:HQ,N:H5,E:H2]

You have won the \HA. Which card do you lead now? [choose-card any:C9,C4,C3]

[showcards W:C2]

West plays low. Which card do you play from dummy? [choose-card CJ]

[showcards E:C6]



If West has \C K x or \C K x x then yes, that's all there is to it. But if he has \C K x x x then you won't have enough entries to your hand unless you take the first \C finesse <b>BEFORE</b> you start on trumps.

That is why you win the \HA and immediately play a \C to dummy's \CJ, which holds the trick. Then pull trumps, (it takes 4 rounds), ending in your hand.

Click NEXT. [NEXT]

[PLAY W:C2,E:C6,N:SA,E:S2,S:S3,W:S6,N:SQ,E:S4,S:S5,W:H3,N:SJ,E:S8,S:S7,W:HT,N:S9,E:ST,S:SK,W:D2]



Which card do you lead now? [choose-card CT]

[showcards W:C7]

West plays low again. Which card do you play from dummy? [choose-card C5]

[showcards E:H4]

Your \C10, putting on the \C5 from dummy when West plays low again. This lets you stay in your hand to play another \C to the \CQ, picking up all four \C tricks and the slam.

Clickfor the complete Deal. [NEXT]

